<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Drawing a constraint</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>To draw \({@shown@}\) on a graph:</p><p>Give exact values, for example \(4.5\).</p><p>(a) The boundary line crosses the \(x\)-axis at \(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] and the \(y\)-axis at \(y =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The boundary line is drawn [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p><div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Does \((0, 0)\) satisfy the inequality? [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</p><div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) In this book we shade the unwanted side of each line. Which side do you shade? [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</p><div>[[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) On the \(x\)-axis \(y = 0\), so \({@ca@}x = {@cc@}\) and \(x = {@xi@}\). On the \(y\)-axis \(x = 0\), so \({@cb@}y = {@cc@}\) and \(y = {@yi@}\). Draw the line through \(({@xi@}, 0)\) and \((0, {@yi@})\).</p><p>(b) The sign is {@relw@}: it {@incl@}.</p><p>(c) At \((0, 0)\), \({@ca@}x + {@cb@}y = 0\), and \({@zs@}\) is {@tv@}.</p><p>(d) Shade the side where the inequality is false: {@shw@}. Shade what you cannot have, and what is left is what you can.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: draw the boundary, test a point, choose the side; the unwanted side is shaded. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Higher 2, Chapter 1, Section C. Relations <= 3, < 2, >= 3, > 2; entries 5 and 8 shown the other way round. */
Q21L: [[4,9,"<=",54,"4x + 9y \\le 54","0 \\le 54"],
[3,8,"<",24,"3x + 8y \\lt 24","0 \\lt 24"],
[7,2,">=",35,"7x + 2y \\ge 35","0 \\ge 35"],
[6,5,">",90,"6x + 5y \\gt 90","0 \\gt 90"],
[2,7,"<=",63,"63 \\ge 2x + 7y","63 \\ge 0"],
[9,4,">=",54,"9x + 4y \\ge 54","0 \\ge 54"],
[7,8,"<",56,"7x + 8y \\lt 56","0 \\lt 56"],
[8,3,">=",12,"12 \\le 8x + 3y","12 \\le 0"],
[9,2,"<=",27,"9x + 2y \\le 27","0 \\le 27"],
[4,7,">",14,"4x + 7y \\gt 14","0 \\gt 14"]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
E: Q21L[ix];
ca: E[1]; cb: E[2]; rl: E[3]; cc: E[4]; shown: E[5]; zs: E[6];
nsh(v) := block([r], r: floor(rationalize(v)*10^4 + 1/2)/10^4, if integerp(r) then r else float(r));
xi: cc/ca; yi: cc/cb;
sp: is(rl = "<" or rl = ">");
st: if sp then "d" else "s";
ost: if sp then "s" else "d";
org: if rl = "<=" or rl = "<" then "y" else "n";
oorg: if org = "y" then "n" else "y";
sh: if org = "y" then "n" else "o";
osh: if sh = "n" then "o" else "n";
o3: [["s", is(st = "s"), "solid"], ["d", is(st = "d"), "dashed"]];
o4: [["y", is(org = "y"), "yes"], ["n", is(org = "n"), "no"]];
o5: [["o", is(sh = "o"), "the side containing (0, 0)"], ["n", is(sh = "n"), "the side not containing (0, 0)"]];
relt: if rl = "<=" then "\\le" elseif rl = "<" then "\\lt" elseif rl = ">=" then "\\ge" else "\\gt";
relw: if rl = "<=" then "less than or equal to" elseif rl = "<" then "less than" elseif rl = ">=" then "greater than or equal to" else "greater than";
incl: if sp then "does not include the points on the line, so the line is dashed" else "includes the points on the line, so the line is solid";
tv: if org = "y" then "true" else "false";
styw: if sp then "dashed" else "solid";
shw: if sh = "o" then "the side containing \\((0, 0)\\)" else "the side not containing \\((0, 0)\\)";
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
