  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Linear Programming: drawing a constraint</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.4 (b) / Essential 1.4 (b): Find the intercepts of a boundary line, decide solid or dashed, test the origin, and choose the unwanted side to shade.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 1, Section C of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Higher 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: drawing a sloping boundary, testing a point and choosing the side, changed to shading the unwanted side, with new lines.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
