    <node><name>1</name><description>Intercepts swapped</description><answertest>AlgEquiv</answertest><sans>sw1</sans><tans>true</tans><testoptions></testoptions><quiet>0</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-2-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>You have them the wrong way round: \({@ans1@}\) is where the line crosses the \(y\)-axis. On the \(x\)-axis, \(y = 0\).</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>2</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-2-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
    <node><name>2</name><description>Constant not divided</description><answertest>AlgEquiv</answertest><sans>cu1</sans><tans>true</tans><testoptions></testoptions><quiet>0</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-3-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>You typed the constant \({@cc@}\) as an intercept. Check it: [[if test='is(abs(ans1 - cc) < 1/1000)']]at \(({@cc@}, 0)\), \({@ca@}x + {@cb@}y = {@ca*cc@}\), not \({@cc@}\).[[else]]at \((0, {@cc@})\), \({@ca@}x + {@cb@}y = {@cb*cc@}\), not \({@cc@}\).[[/if]] Put the other letter equal to \(0\) and solve the equation that is left.</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>-1</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-3-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Test your values in the equation of the boundary line. At \(({@ans1@}, 0)\), \({@ca@}x + {@cb@}y = {@nsh(ca*ans1)@}\); at \((0, {@ans2@})\), \({@ca@}x + {@cb@}y = {@nsh(cb*ans2)@}\). Both should be \({@cc@}\). Put \(y = 0\) to find where the line crosses the \(x\)-axis, then \(x = 0\) for the \(y\)-axis.</p>]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
